# AlphaLog cron schedule — Lattice variant of the root `crontab`.
#
# Same schedule as the Fly `alphalog-cron` sidecar, adapted for this stack:
# calls the sibling `web` container over the Compose network (`web:3000`)
# instead of Fly's private 6PN (`alphalog-pwa.internal:3000`). CRON_SECRET /
# OPS_CRON_SECRET come from this directory's `.env` (same values as Fly).
#
# Deliberately DOES NOT include the coinarb-50x auto-deploy line from the
# root crontab — coinarb stays on Fly, deployed by Fly's own alphalog-cron.
# Keep this file in sync with the root `crontab` by hand when jobs change
# there (diff the two, swap the hostname) — there isn't enough churn here to
# justify templating them from one source.
#
# Only activate this service once Lattice is the one serving real traffic
# (see the `cron` profile note in docker-compose.yml) — running both this
# and Fly's alphalog-cron against the same Supabase DB at once would double
# some non-idempotent jobs (e.g. business/recurring-costs).

# Terminal / market data
0    *    *  *  *   curl --fail --max-time 60 -X POST -H "x-cron-secret: $CRON_SECRET" http://web:3000/api/terminal/reports/refresh
0    */2  *  *  *   curl --fail --max-time 60 -X POST -H "x-cron-secret: $CRON_SECRET" http://web:3000/api/cron/terminal/news-fetch
*/5  *    *  *  *   curl --fail --max-time 30 -X POST -H "x-cron-secret: $CRON_SECRET" http://web:3000/api/cron/terminal/price-fetch
0    6    *  *  1   curl --fail --max-time 60 -X POST -H "x-cron-secret: $CRON_SECRET" http://web:3000/api/cron/terminal/calendar-fetch

